    description: "Source: a second outside reader (a fresh LLM session given only the help output and the cached files) reviewed a hypergumbo 9.2.0 self-run on 2026-11-13, cache f36c63310c791188/results/c872eb7a7e793eab/ac34c56c06ec1788, made after the fixes from the first review merged. Each claim was re-checked against those files and the code on dev fed15705d7, then measured on 20 repositories that are not hypergumbo (default sketch and --no-source, 8k/32k/128k). Scripts, the 120 sketches and results.txt: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_reader_review2_11142026.\n\nOBSERVED. In the default sketch the Entry Points slots (57 with source, see the sibling item on the ADR-0005 caps) go to example scripts while product entries are hidden:\n- sqlalchemy: \"CLI & Scripts\" shows 29 entries, 24 of them under examples/; \"Library API\" shows 28 and ends \"... and 389 more\".\n- pm2: 27 of the 57 entries shown are under examples/.\n- express: 19 of the 23 are under examples/.\n- hypergumbo self-run: the sixth CLI entry is the main() of a recorded test-input project (packages/hypergumbo-lang-scip-python/recorded/sample_project/pkg/app.py), and one-off measurement scripts fill the rest of the group while 67 library exports are hidden.\nSmaller counts elsewhere: mini-redis 4, prometheus 3, ripgrep 3, alertmanager 2, lazygit 1. The other 12 repositories show none on such paths (path components matched: fixtures, testdata, recorded, samples, examples, demos, benchmarks, bench).\n\nMECHANISM. Two rules that do not meet. entrypoints.py halves the rank of an entry in a utility or example file (is_utility_file, x0.5), which orders entries INSIDE a display group. sketch._share_entry_budget then splits the section's slots between the groups by water-filling: each group gets an even share whatever its entries rank. A library has few real scripts, so the scripts group is filled with half-weight example scripts up to its even share, and the group that holds the library's API is cut to the same share. The rank penalty never gets to compete across groups.\n\nASK. Decide how slots are shared between groups when the groups differ in rank: for example share by the rank mass of each group, or fill by rank across groups with a floor of one entry per group (the floor is what INV-liraj's fix protects: no kind of entry point disappears). Measure on the 20 repositories: entries shown on example or fixture paths and entries hidden in the largest group, before and after.\n\nGENERALITY (owner, 2026-11-13). The fix must be a rule that holds for any repository and any language. The hypergumbo self-run is only where the defect was first seen. A fix keyed to this repository's paths or file names, or one that works for one language only, does not close this item.\nThe rule has to be stated on rank and group, never on a directory name; the directory names above are only how the instances were counted. Related, not the same: WI-fosuk-mudof-fapol-foron-vibif-kalam-gizap-tajov (a recorded fixture directory that no predicate classifies) and WI-mapaj-mirig-guhon-mavav-bujis-madaj-tuguh-fivuz (rank saturation inside a group)."  # 8e7e
